{
  "dom_id": "step-q48688",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The function $x(t)$ models the number of meters traveled by a car, $t$ seconds after it sets off on a journey. What is the best interpretation of ${x}^{′}(30)=10?$",
  "worked_solution": "The function ${x}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of meters is changing at the moment $t$ seconds after starting its journey.\n\nTherefore, ${x}^{′}(30)=10$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second*",
